kobuild recipes and scripts use the MIT license in LICENSE.

The SDK images include third-party software under its own licenses. The MIT
license does not replace the terms of Qt, its patches, or other dependencies.

Qt5 uses the pinned NickelTC image in qt5/Dockerfile. Its upstream recipes,
patches and source references are available at https://github.com/pgaskin/NickelTC.
The exact source revisions of all components in that binary image have not been
verified. The image digest identifies binaries, not a complete source archive.
Debian package notices and package status from NickelTC are retained under
/usr/share/doc/kobuild/nickeltc-packages, nickeltc-common-licenses and
nickeltc-package-status. This metadata covers the upstream image's packages;
it is not an inventory of only the files copied into this SDK.

Qt6 builds the official archive recorded in qt6/source/source.json with the
included patches. The prepared Qt source, patch inputs, license notices and
build scripts are bundled in /usr/src/kobuild/qt6-source.tar.xz. The source
archive includes third-party code bundled in Qt under its original terms.
Qt patch notices are also available at
/usr/share/doc/kobuild/qt6-patches-NOTICE.
Qt Sensors uses the official archive pinned in qt6/sensors.json. Its source,
license texts, checksum manifest and build script are bundled separately in
/usr/src/kobuild/qt6-sensors-source.tar.xz.

Android uses the official Qt binary kits and matching Qt Base and Qt Sensors
source archives recorded with SHA-256 checksums in android/manifest.json.
The source archives are included in /usr/src/kobuild/android. The Qt host kit
also includes ICU 73.2 from Qt's binary archive. Its upstream license from
https://github.com/unicode-org/icu/blob/release-73-2/icu4c/LICENSE is retained as
/usr/share/doc/kobuild/icu-LICENSE.txt.
Qt's installer archive filenames identify the machine that built the Android
libraries; those libraries target Android ARM64, not macOS.

Android SDK, NDK and command-line tools retain their own licenses and notices
under /opt/android-sdk. See https://developer.android.com/studio#terms-and-conditions
for the SDK terms. Building the Android image accepts the SDK package licenses.
The image includes JDK 21 from Ubuntu under its package terms. Application
signing keys are not included.

Qt license texts are included in /usr/share/doc/kobuild/qt-licenses inside all
images. Ubuntu package notices remain in /usr/share/doc. The Qt6 source archive
does not contain the sources for Ubuntu packages or the cross compiler. This
repository is not a complete corresponding-source archive for the whole image.

Application-specific dependencies and patches are not included.
